    "media:imagetext": "Baguio Jan. 26, 1938\nDear A. 0.\nAs you probably know my work in the Orient had largely to do\nwith the establishment of the trans-Pacific service of Pan American.\nThat job was completed last tay with the inaugural flight of the China\nClipper from Tanila to Hongkong, I remained in Shanghai only to permit\none of my associates to return to the Uns. for his furlough before he\nassumed the duties. which I had been performing in connection with the\noperations in China. While my \"number one\" was on home leave the war\nbroke out and\nit was deemed necessary to withdraw all American flight\nand ground personnel\noving to the stupid policies of the Chinese iinis-\nter of Communications who refused to recognize the commercial status of\nthe company and took no action to protect our American pilots - even\ncondoned the act of a young officer in compelling one of our pilots to\ntransport bombs at the point of a gun. It was not long before the\nChinese learned the folly of their ways and we then went to Nanking in\nlate October and early November, negotiated a new deal by going over the\nhead of the ilinister direct to ladam Chiang Kai-shek and Dr. H. H. Kung.\nThe result was the granting of all our requirements, the elimination of\nthe ilinister who had given us so many head aches and also the resignation\nof the llanaging Director who was replaced by our nominee, The company is\nnow operating under the most favorable corporate organization which has\never existed during my five years in China.\nThe war naturally presents\nmany problems most\nof which can be solved\nthrough radio communications.\nAirplanes are in constant touch with terminals and are warned\nof\nan air-\nraid in plenty of time to proceed to another field or loaf around until\nthe \"all clear\" signal is given - then fly\non to destination.\nPlanes are\nbasud at one end\nof\nthe line at Chungking - far inland city which has not\nbeen attacked, and\nat Hongkong which of course is Inglish territory.\nThe\nCNAC has been using a marvelous radio device which permits safe flight to\nan exact\npoint even if the pilot must fly completely \"blind\" for many\nhours and the pilots who used to yearn for good weather are now happy if\nthere is a low solid overcast for once in the clouds no one can attack\nthem - even if\nthey wanted to do so. Ly \"number one\" is now back on the\njob and the Bixby family vill soon be heading homes All concessions in\nManila, Hongkong and Incao are in good shape and my work has been fairly",
    "media:imagetext_created": 1787971994,
